eta ={45}^{∘}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "405bd8b0-536b-5f37-9b2a-88044b8dd73a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339002 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =16\\operatorname{cos}⁡({45}^{∘}) \\\\  & =16\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{4\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{2}}p \\\\  & =2p\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1295->1277. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428209 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186051021 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186441535 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 1759218